<newsitem itemid="187226" id="root" date="1996-11-13" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Hambros swings into pretax profit in H1.</title>
<headline>Hambros swings into pretax profit in H1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  7.2		  vs 10.9 loss</p>
<p> Dividend  (pence)	  2.5		  vs 2.5</p>
<p> Pretax profit		35.0		 vs 7.7 loss</p>
<p> Operating income	   82.5		 vs 93.7</p>
<p> Operating costs	    72.5		 vs 77.8</p>
<p> Bad/doubtful debt charge 5.9		  vs 23.5</p>
<p> Tax paid		     11.2		 vs 8.3</p>
<p> Net taxed		    23.8		 vs 16.0 loss</p>
<p> Net interest income	23.1		 vs 26.4</p>
<p> Pay date		     December 12</p>
<p> Div registration date    December 3</p>
<p> Ex-div date		  November 25</p>
<p>NOTE - British investment banking group Hambros Plc said its corporate finance, structured banking, bonds, cash management and offshore private banking &quot;continue to perform robustly&quot;. It reported &quot;excellent results&quot; from its investment group and &quot;sharply improved performance&quot; from estate agency Hambro Countrywide and Hambro Insurance Services.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
